  "Der Feind ist in die Stadt eingebrochen – der Weg zum Strand ist offen. Die Boote müssen ohne Deckung ablegen.": "The enemy has broken into the town – the way to the beach is open. The boats must cast off without cover.",
  "Die Boote legen ab! Rückzug zum Strand, die Nachhut folgt. Gut gehalten.": "The boats are casting off! Fall back to the beach, the rearguard follows. Well held.",
  "Die Kanallinie hat gehalten. Tausende Soldaten konnten übersetzen.": "The canal line has held. Thousands of soldiers were able to cross.",
  "Der Brückenkopf hielt, bis die Boote abgelegt hatten. In den folgenden Tagen konnten über 330.000 Soldaten die Küste verlassen – die Armee war gerettet, doch ihre Ausrüstung blieb am Strand zurück.": "The bridgehead held until the boats had cast off. In the following days over 330,000 soldiers were able to leave the coast – the army was saved, but its equipment was left behind on the beach.",
